  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The query is a lipophilic 4-hydroxycoumarin (phenprocoumon-type) with a single acidic enol and no basic amine or polyphenolic conjugation motifs. Human oral bioavailability values for transferred small-molecule analogues range from ~32% to 92%, all above the 20% threshold; the only low-F analogue is a poorly transferable polyhydroxyflavone. Thus F >= 20% is better supported.",
